WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.994 --> 00:00:03.382
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:04.840
LARRY P. ARNN: This
graduate school

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.390
was inspired by
George Washington

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.020
to teach the things, the large
things, that a statesman would

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.270
need to know to govern
this country well.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:22.258
MATTHEW SPALDING: What's missing
in a lot of politics today

00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:23.800
is, we have a lot
of people that want

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.177
to talk about first principles.

00:00:25.177 --> 00:00:27.010
And, of course, we have
a lot of people that

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.010
want to focus just on action.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.190
It's connecting the two that's
the virtue of statesmanship.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.140
TOM COTTON: Education
is about more than just

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.182
turning out good workers.

00:00:36.182 --> 00:00:38.840
It should be about turning
out good citizens, as well,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.570
the next generation
of Americans who

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.413
understand the timeless
principles of our government.

00:00:43.413 --> 00:00:45.580
And, unfortunately, too
many schools, and especially

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.560
universities, not only
fail in that mission,

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.373
but they actively
repudiate that mission.

00:00:50.373 --> 00:00:52.540
MOLLIE HEMINGWAY: Young
people who come to this town

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.220
don't have that
founding understanding

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.240
of how government should be
and how it will best operate.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.710
JAMIE DANGERS: So I'm excited
about learning the larger story

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.620
and how to
incorporate the wisdom

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:11.360
of people who came before us
into a very fraught culture

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:11.860
right now.

00:01:14.218 --> 00:01:15.760
MATTHEW SPALDING:
We're going to look

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.170
at core documents,
original documents,

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:21.700
we're going to
study the writings

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.105
and thoughts of great
statesmen and great books.

00:01:24.105 --> 00:01:25.480
LARRY P. ARNN:
And it will mostly

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.240
be taken by people who
work in the government.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.880
And they will read old books.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.450
They'll start with Plato
and Aristotle and Herodotus

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.220
and Thucydides.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.410
And they'll learn
what politics is,

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.610
and then they'll
learn what America is.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.330
Understand how the
Constitution works,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.760
and then it'll teach
the alternatives

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.790
to the Constitution that have
grown up in understanding

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:55.370
and in institutions
in America, that

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.710
are the abnegation
of the Constitution.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.640
And then you'll be equipped
to go out in the world

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:02.690
and make some decisions.

00:02:07.882 --> 00:02:11.330
To be a fine human being, you
need to have good character.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.880
To be a fine human being and
the finest kind of human being,

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.600
you need to understand the
ultimate purposes of life

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.060
and everything else.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.090
And, finally, to be a fine human
being, you need to be free.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.910
We're a college aiming
for all those four things.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.630
And so the way we're
serious about that

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.150
is to teach in ways that
are helpful to being

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.460
better and governing a
free country, the United

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.040
States of America.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.070
We can help ambitious
people to understand

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:47.210
what that is so they can
cultivate it within themselves

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:50.210
and learn from it, and
that is of huge value.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.710
[RAPID DRUM BEATS]

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.960
[MUSIC PLAYING]

